# Project Structure and Test Conventions

## Where to put new code

- **React components:** `src/components/` (e.g. `TownTab.jsx`, `HeroList.jsx`). Group by feature if it grows (e.g. `src/components/town/`, `src/components/hero/`).
- **React hooks:** `src/hooks/` for shared hooks (e.g. `useGameState.js`). Hook files are camelCase; they import from `src/services/` and expose state/actions to components.
- **React app entry / shell:** `src/main.js` loads bootstrap; `src/App.jsx` is the root component. Do not put game logic in the shell; it should wire services and render the tab/route tree.
- **Game logic:** Only in `src/services/`. No new game logic in React components or hooks.
- **Tests:** **Regression is E2E:** run `npm test` (builds then runs Playwright). E2E lives in `e2e/`. Unit tests for store and services live under `src/` (e.g. `*.test.js`); add or extend them when touching services.

## E2E tests (Playwright)

- **Stable selectors:** Prefer `data-testid` for elements that tests need to click or assert on (e.g. `data-testid="gather-button"`, `data-testid="town-tab"`). This keeps tests from breaking when copy or CSS classes change.
- **When adding new UI:** Add a `data-testid` on key interactive elements and use it in E2E. Reserve testids for “contract” points (main actions, tab areas, key headings); don’t add them to every node.
- **Existing tests:** E2E use roles, text, and IDs (e.g. `#gatherButton`, `#resources`). Keep or add testids so the same E2E flow still works; update selectors only when the DOM structure intentionally changes.
